+<h2>128. The info reader and the create path are pinned to carry the same allow-list guard as executable code (KS-1534, item a)</h2>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>What this changes.</strong></td><td> One new test file, <code>Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1534-allow-list-guards-are-the-same-executable-code.test.ts</code> (test only, +57 lines). <code>GET /api/connector/info</code> (<code>services/health.ts</code>) and the create path (<code>routes/verification.ts</code>, KS 1204) each refuse a present allow-list that is not an array with the same guard, <code>if (X !== undefined &amp;&amp; X !== null &amp;&amp; !Array.isArray(X)) {</code>, duplicated rather than shared. The existing agreement cell in <code>ks1232-info-reader-refuses-a-non-array-allow-list.test.ts</code> catches drift in what each route does; this file pins the other half of item (a): that the two guards stay the same <strong>executable code</strong>.
+    </td></tr><tr><td>Five cells. The test reads both sources as text, drops every whole-line comment first (a guard that survives only in a comment is not a guard), and compares the guard condition with the variable name normalised. G1 and G2 are RED-first; G3 to G5 are controls (the create path carries the canonical guard; a commented guard is not counted; the scan can fail on a guard with the array test dropped). <strong>Zero product bytes</strong>: <code>health.ts</code> is the tamper target and is never committed.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3>128.1 What proves it</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>Red under a tamper, green on the untouched product, and no other cell moves.</strong></td><td> <strong>Tamper, worktree only, never committed:</strong> dropping the <code>!Array.isArray(rawAllowedTypes)</code> test from <code>health.ts</code> line 98 makes <strong>2 of 5 fail</strong> (G1 and G2), the 3 controls pass. The file was restored by content and its whole-file sha256 equals the pre-tamper value. <strong>Untouched product:</strong> 5 of 5 pass.
+    </td></tr><tr><td><strong>Whole api-gateway unit suite</strong> (vitest, <code>--maxWorkers=3</code>, warm, run twice): develop <code>a8c554659cb3</code> 130 files / 1321 cells, 1321 pass in both runs; with the change 131 files / <strong>1326 cells, 1326 pass</strong> in both runs, 0 failed, 0 skipped. <code>tsc --noEmit</code> with every test file in the program (167 source files, 131 under <code>__tests__</code>): the new file adds <strong>0 errors</strong>; the program carries 27 errors in 7 other test files, and the same 27 lines at develop (measured at the base). <code>eslint</code> on the test file: 0 errors, 0 warnings, and a planted file raised <code>@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars</code> and <code>no-debugger</code>.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3>128.2 Environment and figures</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="1"><strong>Measured 2026-10-30 (UTC) on an Apple Silicon (arm64) Mac, macOS 27.0.1, shared with other seats.</strong></td><td> Develop <code>a8c554659cb3</code> with the change on top. Node v26.8.1 (not an LTS line), TypeScript 5.9.3, vitest 4.1.12, eslint 10.7.0. The api-gateway suite is load-sensitive on this host, so it was run with <code>--maxWorkers=3</code>, warm, twice.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3>128.3 What this does not prove</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>A text comparison of two files, not a running service.</strong></td><td> KS-1534 stays open. Item (a) is covered by the source-level option only; the helper option (one function imported by both routes) is not done, and item (b), whether an array of non-strings is refused by both read routes together, is a contract question and is untouched. The cells compare text; they do not run the two routes.
+    </td></tr><tr><td>Not run: the four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, Performance/k6), a running stack, Node 24, any deploy.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3>128.4 Running it</h3>
+<pre><code>cd Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway &amp;&amp; npx vitest run src/__tests__/ks1534-allow-list-guards-are-the-same-executable-code.test.ts   # 5 cells in this file
+cd Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway &amp;&amp; npx vitest run --maxWorkers=3         # 131 files / 1326 cells, warm, run twice</code></pre>
